{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794778894,"nonce":"sfyZ1eYMxoJY+h84WyRpZUXsNaA=","title":"A hover change restyles every element that has state rules","message":"`apply_stylesheet_state_styles` walks every registered element id with state styles and calls `apply_state_styles` on each whenever it runs, not only the elements whose hover / active / focus state changed. On the cn_demo page a scroll frame under a still pointer restyled about 58 nodes (174 `set_style` calls), each rebuilding props from the base and resolving its cascades.\n\nSince the epoch fix these restyles no longer count as layout changes, but the CPU is still spent each time hover changes, which during a scroll under a still pointer is every frame.\n\nRestyle only the nodes whose router state changed since the last call (the router knows the previous and current hovered / active sets), plus those whose rules depend on an ancestor's state.","files":null}]}